    "representation": "Reconstructed manuscript rune tokens plus six isolated digits; corpus Unicode-code-point lengths under strict UTF-8 and literal-space tokenization.",
    "procedure": "Audit every pinned files/ path and its first 2902 nonempty tokens when eligible; calculate all 23 exact descriptive ranks under path and distinct-blob weighting; independently check source bytes and ranks.",
    "parameters": "25906 paths; 25844 distinct source blobs; 25565 eligible paths and 25563 eligible blobs; 2902 tokens per prefix; bins 1..14 and 15+; n-1 variance and linear quartiles.",
    "exclusions": "No language identification, random passage sampling, header removal, alphabet filtering, edition deduplication, calibrated p-values or reproduction of the unavailable corpus converter."
  },
  "outcome": "supported",
  "finding": "The census and all 46 comparison rows are independently reproduced. Of 25565 eligible paths, 138 have a smaller length-two proportion than the manuscript and one ties it; all other measures and both weights are retained.",
  "limitations": "A fixed nonrandom collection of prefixes with undocumented conversion and edition provenance. Corpus code points and manuscript runes plus digits are different units. Descriptive ranks do not identify language or cipher. Human review pending.",
  "next_steps": "Any changed converter, rune-only target, passage selection or genre-matched reference needs a separately declared variant; do not reinterpret these ranks as probabilities.",
